+// DeviceProxy: a full delegating wrapper around the real IDirect3DDevice9(Ex).
+//
+// Why a full wrapper instead of vtable patching: the Steam overlay
+// (gameoverlayrenderer.dll) swaps the device object's vtable pointer to its
+// own heap-allocated shadow and restores the original vtable memory, which
+// silently bypasses any in-place vtable patch (verified on the real game).
+// With a wrapper, the game holds OUR object with OUR vtable; nothing can
+// swap or restore it. The 18 intercepted methods forward to the hkXxx
+// detours in DeviceHooks.cpp (which call back into m_real, keeping the
+// overlay in the chain); everything else is a plain forward.
